    Contrast is a floor. WCAG 2.2 asks <strong>4.5:1</strong> for normal text, <strong>3:1</strong> for large text and UI edges (AA); <strong>7:1</strong> is AAA. Every pairing below is measured. Green passes, amber and raw red do not, which is exactly why the darker variants exist.
