  <p>
    WCAG 2.2 contrast floors SC 1.4.3 / 1.4.6 / 1.4.11 and use of color SC 1.4.1 (<a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">w3.org/TR/WCAG22</a>). Role-token model after Material 3 color roles (<a href="https://m3.material.io/styles/color/roles">m3.material.io</a>) and Refactoring UI numbered scales. The primitive color ramps are Tailwind CSS’s open-source (MIT) default palette (<a href="https://tailwindcss.com/docs/colors">tailwindcss.com</a>), adopted hex-for-hex as the raw material; the role concepts and numbered scales come from Material 3 and Refactoring UI. The 60-30-10 accent balance is a common color composition rule. Ratios computed with the WCAG 2.x relative-luminance formula, matching the Color Picker story.
